{"raw": {"https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1580": {"title": "Shuttle Drivers (Part-Time)", "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Shuttle Drivers (Part-Time) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Shuttle Drivers (Part-Time) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Shuttle Drivers (Part-Time) Posting Number 20110431 Pay Rate $10.00/hour Position Type Part Time/Temporary Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Shuttle Van Drivers are responsible for the safe, timely and professional transportation of employees, visitors, guests and students to and from various locations. Ranging from 15, 12 and 5 passenger vehicles. Responsibilities include: \u2022 Able to work well independently with minimal supervision. \u2022 Able to work flexible hours, including mornings, evenings and weekends, part-time work. \u2022 Greet and welcome passengers in a friendly professional welcoming manner. \u2022 Maintain a neat and professional appearance at all times. \u2022 Maintain operation of vehicle; fuel vehicle as needed. \u2022 Report suspected maintenance issues with vehicle to supervisor at end of shift. \u2022 Observe and abide all Federal and State traffic regulations in the respective states in which operating. \u2022 Observe all safety laws and ensure passengers adhere to all safety laws. \u2022 Assist passengers with placing and securing personal belongings safely in the vehicle. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status .\u2026EOE Position Qualifications Drivers must have a valid driver\u2019s license for a minimum of 2 years and a good driving record (no major driving convictions accepted, no minor offenses within 5 years.) Drivers must be at least 21 years of age to apply. Child Abuse and Criminal Background checks and MVR will be completed. Drivers must be flexible as, we run shuttles 7 days per week. This could include daily runs, or monthly shuttles. Drivers are scheduled as needed all hours are on a part-time basis. Successful candidates must complete online safety training and pass a behind the wheel assessment. Supervision Required/Given This position reports to the Transportation Coordinator/ Supervisor. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/07/2022 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Walk-In Government Employment Agency Private Employment Agency Employee (please explain in follow up question) Relative (please explain in follow up question) School Advertisement - Source (please explain in follow up question) Other (please explain in follow up question) If you were referred by a person, advertisement or other, please explain here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1769": {"title": "Chemistry Outreach Coordinator", "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Chemistry Outreach Coordinator Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Chemistry Outreach Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Why Join Us? At Juniata College, you'll be part of a passionate team bringing quality STEM education to communities that need it most. If you're looking to make a difference in the lives of students and teachers\u2014and have a background in science education\u2014this is the role for you! Apply today to be a key part of our mission-driven outreach team. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Chemistry Outreach Coordinator Posting Number 20110652 Pay Rate Starting at $23,160 (over 10 mos) Position Type Part Time/Temporary Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Join Juniata College\u2019s nationally recognized Science In Motion ( SIM ) program as a Part-time Chemistry Outreach Coordinator and help bring hands-on, high-impact science education to local school districts. The Chemistry Outreach Coordinator plays a vital role in sustaining and expanding SIM\u2019s chemistry-focused outreach efforts. This part-time position is essential to maintaining our existing partnerships and fulfilling contractual commitments to participating schools. Key Responsibilities: Provide Science In Motion ( SIM ) chemistry education services 3 days per week in accordance with Pennsylvania Department of Education ( PDE ) contracts Coordinate and implement outreach initiatives and lab programs for local schools Hire, train, and supervise Juniata College student employees Oversee the scheduling, delivery, and maintenance of outreach equipment Serve as a consultant to local teachers to support and enhance science education in the classroom The Chemistry Outreach Coordinator is a part time 10-month position with no benefits and annual renewal based upon performance and funding. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status ..\u2026EOE Position Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in Chemistry, Education, or a related scientific discipline Excellent organizational and time-management skills Strong interpersonal and written communication skills Ability to work independently and as part of a team Understanding of Juniata College\u2019s mission and outreach vision Valid driver\u2019s license required, clear of major violations. Juniata College reserves the right to review driving records to determine suitability for position. Supervision Required/Given This role reports directly to the Outreach Director and works collaboratively with other STEM coordinators on campus. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working in educational outreach or similar programs Pennsylvania teaching certification Classroom teaching experience Physical Demands Ability to unload and reload vehicle, push/pull loaded carts, usually lift up to 20-lbs and sometimes up to 50-lbs. Special Instructions to Applicants Why Join Us? At Juniata College, you\u2019ll be part of a passionate team bringing quality STEM education to communities that need it most. If you\u2019re looking to make a difference in the lives of students and teachers\u2014and have a background in science education\u2014this is the role for you! Apply today to be a key part of our mission-driven outreach team. Posting Detail Information Open Date 02/05/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1840": {"title": "Assistant Field Hockey Coach", "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Assistant Field Hockey Coach Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Field Hockey Coach Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. It is Juniata College\u2019s policy to conduct background checks. Valid driver\u2019s license required, clear of major violations. Juniata College reserves the right to review driving records to determine suitability for position. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Field Hockey Coach Posting Number 20110679 Pay Rate Monthly stipend plus room and board Position Type Administration Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Juniata College, an NCAA Division III Institution, invites applications for a full-time Assistant Field Hockey Coach-Intern. This is a 12-month position that includes a monthly stipend, room, board and full benefits. Juniata is a co-educational, liberal arts college and highly regarded for its academic excellence. Responsibilities include but are not limited to; assisting the Head Field Hockey Coach with all operations of the field hockey program, including but not limited to, recruiting, athlete and team development, practice planning, academic monitoring, team travel and meet management. Key Responsibilities: Leading recruiting responsibilities: \u201cRecruiting Coordinator\u201d \u2013 communication with PSAs, database management, visit planning, and calendar scheduling. Coordinating travel arrangements: meals, lodging, practices. Supporting all practice and match preparations. Conducting individual workouts and team skill development sessions. Contributing to scouting, game-day strategy, and in-game decision making. Assisting with summer camps, fundraising, and alumni engagement. Participating in departmental functions and committee work as needed. Supporting athletic operations and game-day management. Other duties as assigned by the Athletic Director/Field Hockey Coach. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status\u2026 EOE Position Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s Degree required One to Three years of collegiate coaching &/or playing experience preferred Knowledge and understanding of NCAA (and Landmark Conference) rules, regulations, and the Division III philosophy. Demonstrated ability to coach, recruit, manage, and contribute to a competitive college field hockey program. Valid driver\u2019s license required, clear of major violations. Juniata College reserves the right to review driving records to determine suitability for position. Supervision Required/Given This position reports to the Head Field Hockey Coach. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants It is Juniata College\u2019s policy to conduct background checks. Valid driver\u2019s license required, clear of major violations. Juniata College reserves the right to review driving records to determine suitability for position. Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/08/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1848": {"title": "Custodian", "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Custodian Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Custodian Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applicants must complete our online application form. No phone calls or walk-ins please. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Custodian Posting Number 20110673 Pay Rate $17.84/hour Position Type Facilities Services Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Juniata College invites applicants for one open Custodian position, Wednesday-Sunday, 7a-3p. Under general supervision, performs necessary duties to keep assigned buildings and/or areas in clean, neat and orderly condition. Performs various other activities as assigned. Clears snow and ice from, but not limited to, stairs, walks, driveways and College roads either manually or using motorized equipment. Performs necessary repairs and routine and planned maintenance on custodial equipment. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status \u2026 EOE Position Qualifications -Experience in custodial or related field -High school graduate or GED , as well as the ability to read, write and perform basic math -Ability to operate all College owned vehicles and custodial equipment -Valid PA driver\u2019s license, clear of major violations. It is the policy of Juniata College to conduct background checks. Supervision Required/Given Oral and/or written instructions received from designated supervisor. Employees in this classification have no supervisory duties. Preferred Qualifications See position qualifications Physical Demands -Ability to push, pull and lift 40lbs regularly -Ability to work on ladders at heights of 10\u2019 Special Instructions to Applicants All applicants must complete our online application form. No phone calls or walk-ins please. Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/13/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1610": {"title": "Part-time Public Safety Officer", "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Part-time Public Safety Officer Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Part-time Public Safety Officer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Part-time Public Safety Officer Posting Number 20110589 Pay Rate Position Type Part Time/Temporary Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Juniata College invites applicants for a Part-time Public Safety Officer position. Qualified applicants will assure protection of College assets and campus community as well as enforcement of College policies and laws within the jurisdiction of Juniata College. Days and hours vary from 16 to 32 hours per week. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status ..\u2026EOE Position Qualifications Must be available to work second or third shift, weekends and holidays, have a minimum of 1 year professional experience in security or law enforcement, and be able to obtain Act 235 certification. Selected candidates must be highly motivated, with strong interpersonal and communication skills, ability to exercise sound judgment and remain calm in difficult situations, a working knowledge of computers, ability to complete detailed reports and investigations, be physically able to fulfill duties associated with the positions responsibilities. Must have a valid driver\u2019s license. Must understand the importance of working in a diverse community. Supervision Required/Given This position will report to the Director of Public Safety and to the Patrol Supervisors. Preferred Qualifications See Position Qualifications Physical Demands Must be able to lift up to 50 pounds, as required. Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Detail Information Open Date 03/14/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Walk-In Government Employment Agency Private Employment Agency Employee (please explain in follow up question) Relative (please explain in follow up question) School Advertisement - Source (please explain in follow up question) Other (please explain in follow up question) If you were referred by a person, advertisement or other, please explain here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1834": {"title": "Head Women&#39;s Lacrosse Coach", "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Head Women&#39;s Lacrosse Coach Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Head Women's Lacrosse Coach Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Juniata\u2019s Full-Time Benefits package prioritizes the well-being and work-life balance of employees: Medical; vision; dental; retirement (403b); paid vacation, sick leave, holiday time; tuition benefit (employee, spouse and dependents); wellness programming; and additional insurance programs. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Head Women's Lacrosse Coach Posting Number 20110676 Pay Rate Starting at $53,400 Position Type Administration Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Juniata College invites applications for the position of Head Women\u2019s Lacrosse Coach. Juniata is a co-educational, liberal arts college, highly regarded for its academic excellence, with an enrollment of 1,300 students. Juniata is a founding member of the highly regarded Landmark Conference, which is committed to conducting intercollegiate athletics programs in a way that recognizes, as paramount, the centrality of the academic mission at each member institution. Primary Role: Responsible for the development and maintenance of the lacrosse program. This includes structural and administrative organization of the program as outlined below. Typical Duties and Responsibilities: \u00b7 Provide vision and build a positive team culture committed to the welfare of our student-athletes, a positive representation of the college, academic excellence, citizenship, and competitive success. \u00b7 Practice organization, planning, scheduling, preparation, and execution. \u00b7 Develop and implement specific training and skill development programs. \u00b7 Prepare the team for competitions including; scouting reports, meetings, and instruction. \u00b7 Develop and implement appropriate in-competition coaching techniques and strategies. \u00b7 Recruit and retain qualified student-athletes. \u00b7 Develop and meet recruiting goals in consultation with the Director of Athletics. \u00b7 Maintain roster sizes in accordance with agreed upon maximum and minimum roster ranges. \u00b7 Provide support, oversight, assistance, to student-athletes with regards to academic performance, planning, and success. \u00b7 Meet department standards for academic success. \u00b7 Effectively manage all aspects of the program\u2019s budget including the purchase of all athletic equipment and supplies, and the management of the programs travel and recruiting budgets. \u00b7 Hire, train, mentor, assistant coaches, student-assistants, and student managers. \u00b7 Schedule all non-traditional and traditional competitions and practices. \u00b7 Develop, recommend, and enforce appropriate levels of discipline, behavior, rules, regulations, and conduct. \u00b7 Serve as team spokesman and appropriately represent the program and the college on campus and in the community. \u00b7 Ensure adherence to the rules, regulations, and policies of all governing bodies\u2014Juniata College Athletics, Juniata College, Landmark Conference, and National Collegiate Athletic Association. \u00b7 Participate in overall administration of the Athletics Department by representing the office as requested and cooperatively assisting colleagues. This includes attending all mandatory department activities and functions, membership on department and campus committees, and participation upon request in enrollment, fundraising, and/or promotional events. \u00b7 Serve as game/event manager as requested. \u00b7 Other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status ..\u2026EOE Position Qualifications \u00b7 Knowledge and capabilities normally acquired through completion of a Bachelor\u2019s Degree or an equivalent combination of education and experience. \u00b7 Knowledge and understanding of NCAA rules, regulations, and the Division III philosophy. \u00b7 Three to five years of collegiate coaching &/or playing experience. \u00b7 Demonstrated ability to teach, strategize, recruit, lead, manage, represent, and oversee a nationally competitive athletic program. - Valid driver\u2019s license required, clear of major violations. Juniata College reserves the right to review driving records to determine suitability for position. - Must achieve satisfactory results from a background check Supervision Required/Given Receives direct supervision from the Director of Athletics. Works collaboratively and supportively with other individuals and groups. Hires, trains, and supervises assistant coaches, and student coaches, student managers, providing specific direction and oversight of assignments and responsibilities. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants Juniata\u2019s Full-Time Benefits package prioritizes the well-being and work-life balance of employees: Medical; vision; dental; retirement (403b); paid vacation, sick leave, holiday time; tuition benefit (employee, spouse and dependents); wellness programming; and additional insurance programs. Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/16/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume List of 3 References Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1843": {"title": "Director of Public Safety", "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Director of Public Safety Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Director of Public Safety Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Why Juniata? At Juniata, public safety is about more than responding to incidents\u2014it\u2019s about building a campus environment where people feel safe, supported, and able to thrive. The Director will have an opportunity to shape campus safety practices, strengthen partnerships across the College, and contribute to the overall student experience. Comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, retirement (403b), paid vacation and holidays, tuition benefits for employees and dependents, wellness programs, and more. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Director of Public Safety Posting Number 20110680 Pay Rate Salary commensurate with experience Position Type Administration Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Juniata College is seeking a collaborative, experienced leader to serve as Director of Public Safety . This position provides strategic and operational leadership for campus safety and security, helping create a safe, welcoming environment where students, faculty, and staff can live, learn, and work. Reporting to the Vice President for Student Life and Dean of Students, the Director leads Public Safety personnel and operations while partnering across campus and with local law enforcement, emergency services, and community agencies. What You\u2019ll Do Lead the daily operations, staffing, training, supervision, and professional development of Public Safety personnel supporting a 24/7 campus operation. Develop and implement strategies, policies, and procedures that promote campus safety, security, emergency preparedness, and crime prevention. Serve as the College\u2019s Clery compliance officer, overseeing crime reporting, Campus Security Authority ( CSA ) training, and related federal and state requirements. Coordinate the College\u2019s emergency communications and emergency operations efforts, serving as a key liaison with law enforcement, fire, EMS , and emergency dispatch agencies. Partner with Student Life and other campus leaders on student conduct, crisis response, investigations, and after-hours emergency situations. Plan security and emergency response for campus events and provide safety training and education to students, faculty, and staff. Build collaborative relationships with victim advocacy and support services and promote trauma-informed responses to incidents. Develop and manage the Public Safety budget and ensure effective stewardship of departmental resources. Oversee departmental communications, reporting, records, crime statistics, policies, and compliance documentation. Foster a culture of belonging, inclusion, respect, and well-being throughout campus. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status ..\u2026EOE Position Qualifications What We\u2019re Looking For Bachelor\u2019s degree in criminal justice, social work, student affairs, or a related field; advanced study or equivalent professional experience preferred. 5\u20137+ years of progressively responsible experience in public safety, law enforcement, campus safety, student affairs, or a related field. Demonstrated experience supervising personnel and managing departmental budgets and operations. Knowledge of the Clery Act, Title IX, VAWA , Title VII , and applicable federal, state, and local safety requirements. Experience with emergency management, crisis response, investigations, and/or campus safety programming. Strong interpersonal, communication, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work effectively with students, families, faculty, staff, administrators, and external partners. A collaborative, inclusive, and transparent leadership style with a demonstrated ability to build trust and foster positive change. Commitment to the residential liberal arts college experience and to creating a safe and supportive campus community. Valid driver\u2019s license and successful completion of a background investigation. Supervision Required/Given Reports directly to the Vice President for Student Life and Dean of Students. Receives general direction and guidance while working with independent discretion. Direct supervision of full-time and part-time public safety officers and personnel. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants Why Juniata? At Juniata, public safety is about more than responding to incidents\u2014it\u2019s about building a campus environment where people feel safe, supported, and able to thrive. The Director will have an opportunity to shape campus safety practices, strengthen partnerships across the College, and contribute to the overall student experience. Comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, retirement (403b), paid vacation and holidays, tuition benefits for employees and dependents, wellness programs, and more. Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/31/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1854": {"title": "Provost", "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Provost Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Provost Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications, Nominations, and Inquiries Academic Search is partnering with Juniata College in this search . Confidential discussions about the position are welcome and may be arranged by contacting Senior Consultant Dr. Stuart Dorsey: Stuart.Dorsey@academicsearch.org Applications may be submitted at the following link: https://www.academicsearch.org/JuniataProvostApply . A search profile with detailed information about Juniata College, leadership agenda, and required and preferred qualifications for the next provost is available for download here . Nominations and inquiries may be sent to JuniataProvost@academicsearch.org . To apply, candidates should submit two separate documents (in PDF format): (1) a detailed cover letter, addressed to the Search Committee, expressing interest in this position and addressing how you meet the qualifications as outlined in the search profile, and (2) a current resume/curriculum vitae. The position will remain open until filled but only applications received by November 2, 2006. Applications may be submitted at the following link: https://www.academicsearch.org/JuniataProvostApply . Posting Details Position Information Job Title Provost Posting Number 20110684 Pay Rate Salary commensurate with experience and qualifications Position Type Administration Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Academic Search is partnering with Juniata College in this search . Confidential discussions about the position are welcome and may be arranged by contacting Senior Consultant Dr. Stuart Dorsey: Stuart.Dorsey@academicsearch.org Juniata College\u2019s new provost will join an institution ranked among the nation\u2019s top 100 liberal arts colleges and supported by a stable financial outlook and consistent leadership. Dr. James Troha is entering his 14th year as president, and the current provost, Dr. Lauren Bowen, is in her 13th year. Juniata\u2019s faculty and staff are exceptionally student-centered, and its liberal arts academic model is distinctively interdisciplinary. The College seeks a new provost with strong and compelling academic credentials who will advance academic quality and inspire excellence in teaching and learning. The new provost must have exceptional budget management skills and be able to make decisions, communicate with openness, honesty, and transparency, engage stakeholders in meaningful dialogue, and manage change with empathy. As a member of the senior leadership team, the provost will serve as the chief advocate for faculty and academic programs and as a key partner to the president in institutional decision-making. The provost will be the clear leader, advocate, mentor, and public face of the faculty and academic program, maintaining a highly visible and accessible presence across the College. As Juniata\u2019s chief academic officer, the provost reports to the president and provides visionary leadership for the academic enterprise, advancing academic excellence and innovation while strengthening the College\u2019s longstanding tradition of individualized education. Applications may be submitted at the following link: https://www.academicsearch.org/JuniataProvostApply . A search profile with detailed information about Juniata College, leadership agenda, and required and preferred qualifications for the next provost is available for download here . Position Qualifications An earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution. A record of academic achievement, scholarship, and professional accomplishment sufficient to earn the respect and credibility of faculty colleagues. A minimum of five years of progressively responsible academic leadership experience in higher education, such as service as a department chair, division head, dean, associate dean, associate provost, or in a comparable leadership role. A search profile with detailed information about Juniata College, leadership agenda, and required and preferred qualifications for the next provost is available for download here . Supervision Required/Given Reflecting the breadth of the academic enterprise, direct reports to the provost include the associate provost, the assistant vice president of institutional effectiveness, the director of the learning commons, the museum director, the dean of international education, the director of Baker Institute, the laboratory coordinator, the director of community engaged learning, the registrar, the director of advising, the director of the Raystown Field Station, and the assistant to the provost. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants Applications, Nominations, and Inquiries Academic Search is partnering with Juniata College in this search . Confidential discussions about the position are welcome and may be arranged by contacting Senior Consultant Dr. Stuart Dorsey: Stuart.Dorsey@academicsearch.org Applications may be submitted at the following link: https://www.academicsearch.org/JuniataProvostApply . A search profile with detailed information about Juniata College, leadership agenda, and required and preferred qualifications for the next provost is available for download here . Nominations and inquiries may be sent to JuniataProvost@academicsearch.org . To apply, candidates should submit two separate documents (in PDF format): (1) a detailed cover letter, addressed to the Search Committee, expressing interest in this position and addressing how you meet the qualifications as outlined in the search profile, and (2) a current resume/curriculum vitae. The position will remain open until filled but only applications received by November 2, 2006. Applications may be submitted at the following link: https://www.academicsearch.org/JuniataProvostApply . Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/12/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}}, "rows": {"https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1580": {"